spec=R/'docs/phase575_schema_harness_preload_repair_spec.md';spec.write_text('''# Phase575 immutable schema-harness preload repair\n\n## 1. Requirements\nPreserve574 Source, vectors, plan and actual failure. No control passed: schema evaluation stopped on its first dataclasses import before any API call. This is our audit-preload defect, not candidate behavior or platform permission refusal. Prepare only; Root must release a new execution.\n\n## 2. Design\nOnly add explicit dataclasses import before audit installation and change phase namespace/output paths. Keep the exact Source,22 vectors,8 groups,9 positive/13 expected rejects, all assertions and strict audit scope. AST inspection lists every schema import and all dataclasses imports; inspect dependencies load through normal dataclasses import before audit. typing is neither imported by the schema nor lazily imported by dataclasses; no broad stdlib permission is added.\n\n## 3. Realize\nNew tests/phase575_independent_schema_controls.py, exact-byte vector copy and new pins/execution plan. Whole function AST bodies equal574 after phase namespace normalization. One fresh Python -I -B process, cwd/tmp; inner15s/outer20s; fixed new data/phase575-independent-controls-first-001. First unexpected exception stops and preserves evidence without retry. No SUT imports, compile or controls during preparation.\n\n## 4. Acceptance\nFuture released batch repeats all22 unexecuted controls once; completed574 controls remain0. Cumulative schema eval attempts at most2; first attempt did not complete. Legacy result.schema_imports is an attempt counter incremented before exec, so completion must be reported explicitly from the execution trace/case entry. Model/Godot/Native/Expected/pool/wholecapture calls remain0. Successful schema tests would be synthetic Source validation only, not actual Native eligibility.\n''')
